# /opt/inflect/.env.pipelock: the pipelock mediator's environment, and nothing
# else (#5308, owner decision 2026-11-14).
#
# deploy/docker-compose.pipelock.yml loads THIS file through `env_file:`, which
# hands the container every variable in it. It used to load `.env.prod`, which
# put DATA_ENCRYPTION_KEY (the master key over every tenant's DEK), the
# database and Redis credentials and AUTH_SECRET into a third-party image's
# environment. So this file holds only what pipelock needs, and never:
#
#   - DATA_ENCRYPTION_KEY or DATA_ENCRYPTION_KEY_PREVIOUS;
#   - any other line of .env or .env.prod (never copy that file as a start);
#   - pipelock's PRIVATE signing key, which is a bind-mounted file
#     (./pipelock-signing.key), not a variable.
#
# On the VM: root-owned, mode 0600, beside .env.prod:
#
#   sudo install -m 0600 -o root -g root /dev/null /opt/inflect/.env.pipelock
#   sudoedit /opt/inflect/.env.pipelock
#
# deploy/apply.sh refuses to act on the overlay while the file is absent, and
# deploy/check-drift.sh reports it as a credential if it is ever readable
# beyond root. This template is public; the real file is a secret.
#
# READ BEFORE FILLING IN. Only the two variables in section 1 are named by this
# repository, and even those are this repository's reading of the pinned
# release rather than something it has verified (the overlay's own note: the
# exact env and flags depend on the pipelock release in use). The names in
# sections 2 and 3 are PLACEHOLDERS, prefixed UNCONFIRMED__ so that nothing
# reads them by accident: nothing in this repository says what the release at
# the pinned digest (`image:` in deploy/docker-compose.pipelock.yml) calls its
# upstream target or its receipt sink. Confirm each against that release's
# documentation, replace the placeholder name, and only then enable the
# overlay. Several may turn out to be flags or a config-file key rather than
# variables; then they leave this file.

# ── 1. Set inline in the overlay's `environment:` ──────────────────────────
# Kept there rather than here: neither is a secret, and `environment:` wins
# over `env_file:`, so a line here would be silently overridden. Listed for
# completeness only.
#
# PIPELOCK_MODE=balanced                      # detect + sign; "strict" blocks
# PIPELOCK_SIGNING_KEY_FILE=/run/secrets/pipelock-signing.key

# ── 2. The upstream MCP server pipelock mediates ───────────────────────────
# NAME UNCONFIRMED — confirm against the pinned digest's documentation.
# The MCP endpoint pipelock forwards agent tool calls to after inspecting them.
# For Inflect's own MCP surface that is the app on the compose network
# (the app serves on port 3000; the MCP route is /api/mcp). Not a secret.
#
# UNCONFIRMED__UPSTREAM_MCP_URL=http://app:3000/api/mcp

# ── 3. Where receipts are posted, and the key that posts them ──────────────
# NAMES UNCONFIRMED — confirm against the pinned digest's documentation.
# pipelock POSTs each signed CORE receipt to
#
#   POST /api/t/<tenant slug>/agent-receipts
#
# authenticated as a machine caller with `Authorization: Bearer <TenantApiKey>`
# (an `iflk_…` key minted under Admin → API keys in that tenant). The receipt's
# own Ed25519 signature is what the app trusts; the key only authenticates the
# transport and names the tenant.
#
# The KEY is a secret, and the reason this file must stay root-only. Note:
# `agent-receipts` maps to no scope resource in
# src/lib/auth/api-key-path-scope.ts, so today only a key with full access
# (`*`) reaches the route; a narrower key is refused 403. Whether to map the
# route to a scope is an open question, not something to settle by minting a
# `*` key without asking.
#
# UNCONFIRMED__RECEIPT_URL=http://app:3000/api/t/<tenant slug>/agent-receipts
# UNCONFIRMED__RECEIPT_BEARER_TOKEN=
